# Goal-Driven Execution

Every task needs a verifiable success criterion before coding. If it is vague, make it specific or ask.

Examples:
- "Add validation" → reject missing/invalid email, return 400 with a field message, test both cases
- "Fix the bug" → failing repro test, then pass, then existing tests still pass
- "Improve performance" → profile, fix the bottleneck, measure again

For multi-step work, state the plan first (migration, model, endpoint, validation, tests, regression run) so mistakes can be caught before implementation.
